      "parts": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\"The existing NuttX build for the STM32H7 family lacks a complete hardware abstraction for the Nucleo‑H745ZI development board, which prevents applications from accessing key peripherals such as the analog‑to‑digital converter, general‑purpose I/O, multi‑channel PWM, quadrature encoder inputs, and USB host/device functionality. Users attempting to run simulations or real‑time code on this board encounter missing driver implementations and configuration gaps, leading to initialization failures or undefined behavior when peripheral APIs are invoked.\n\nImplement a comprehensive board support package for the Nucleo‑H745ZI that provides functional drivers for the ADC, GPIO, PWM, quadrature encoder, and USB subsystems. The ADC driver must correctly set up the peripheral clock, taking into account the different revision‑specific maximum frequencies, and must ensure that any internal configuration registers are initialized to a known safe state before being modified. The GPIO driver should expose standard pin configuration and read/write operations. The PWM driver must support multi‑channel operation and allow timer‑based output generation. The quadrature encoder driver should enable counting of encoder pulses using the appropriate timer resources. The USB driver must support both host and device modes, handling power control, over‑current detection, and suspend/resume callbacks.\n\nIn addition to the driver implementations, provide a board‑level initialization routine that registers these peripherals with the NuttX device framework based on the selected configuration options. The routine should respect the build‑time configuration flags that enable or disable each subsystem, and it must gracefully handle cases where a peripheral is not configured, returning appropriate error codes. Finally, ensure that the ADC clock setup logic initializes any temporary variables to a defined value before they are used, eliminating the risk of undefined behavior during clock configuration.\"\n",
          "id": "prt_eddf827c2001oSH7Zf0j0U0SEJ",
          "sessionID": "ses_12207d858ffeDYrvGtOrd3NSfT",
          "messageID": "msg_eddf827c10016gqZdl4AJuMSTX"
        }
      ]
