            "input": {
              "description": "Explore NuttX STM32H7 structure",
              "prompt": "Explore the NuttX codebase structure to understand:\n1. Find the existing STM32H7 board support directory structure (look for boards/arm/stm32h7 or similar)\n2. Find existing board initialization patterns (look for stm32_boardinit.c or similar files)\n3. Find existing ADC, GPIO, PWM, encoder, and USB driver implementations for STM32H7\n4. Look for Kconfig files to understand configuration options\n5. Find the Nucleo-H745ZI board directory if it exists\n\nReport back the directory structure, key file locations, and any existing Nucleo-H745ZI related files. Be thorough - search for patterns like \"nucleo\", \"h745\", \"stm32h7\" in file paths and content.",
              "subagent_type": "explore"
            },
            "output": "task_id: ses_1220770abffeng5z3wAbdgZ2DU (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\n\n\nNow I have a comprehensive understanding of the NuttX codebase structure for STM32H7. Let me compile my findings into a detailed report.\n\n## Summary: NuttX STM32H7 Board Support Structure\n\nBased on my thorough exploration of the NuttX codebase, here is a comprehensive report on the STM32H7 board support structure:\n\n---\n\n### 1. STM32H7 Board Support Directory Structure\n\n**Location:** `/workspace/boards/arm/stm32h7/`\n\nThe STM32H7 directory contains **6 board implementations**:\n\n```\nboards/arm/stm32h7/\n├── linum-stm32h753bi/       # Linum STM32H753BI board\n├── nucleo-h743zi/           # Nucleo-H743ZI (single core M7)\n├── nucleo-h743zi2/          # Nucleo-H743ZI2 (updated version)\n├── nucleo-h745zi/           # Nucleo-H745ZI (dual core M7+M4) ⭐\n├── stm32h745i-disco/        # STM32H745I-DISCO (dual core)\n└── stm32h747i-disco/        # STM32H747I-DISCO (dual core)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Nucleo-H745ZI Board Directory (EXISTS)\n\n**Full Path:** `/workspace/boards/arm/stm32h7/nucleo-h745zi/`\n\n**Directory Structure:**\n```\nnucleo-h745zi/\n├── CMakeLists.txt\n├── Kconfig\n├── configs/\n│   ├── nsh_cm4/              # Cortex-M4 core NSH config\n│   │   └── defconfig\n│   ├── nsh_cm4_rptun/        # M4 with RPMsg/RTun support\n│   │   └── defconfig\n│   ├── nsh_cm7/              # Cortex-M7 core NSH config\n│   │   └── defconfig\n│   └── nsh_cm7_rptun/        # M7 with RPMsg/RTun support\n│       └── defconfig\n├── include/\n│   └── board.h               # Board configuration header\n├── scripts/\n│   ├── Make.defs\n│   ├── flash.ld              # M7 flash linker script\n│   └── flash_m4.ld           # M4 flash linker script\n└── src/\n    ├── CMakeLists.txt\n    ├── Makefile\n    ├── nucleo-h745zi.h       # Board-specific definitions\n    ├── stm32_appinitialize.c\n    ├── stm32_autoleds.c      # LED support (CONFIG_ARCH_LEDS)\n    ├── stm32_boot.c          # Boot initialization\n    ├── stm32_bringup.c       # Board bring-up\n    └── stm32_userleds.c      # User LED driver (!CONFIG_ARCH_LEDS)\n```\n\n**Key Configuration:**\n- **Kconfig Symbol:** `CONFIG_ARCH_BOARD_NUCLEO_H745ZI`\n- **Chip Dependencies:** `CONFIG_ARCH_CHIP_STM32H745ZI`\n- **Dual Core Support:** Both Cortex-M7 and Cortex-M4 configurations\n- **RPMsg/RPMsg UART:** Supported for inter-core communication\n\n---\n\n### 3. Existing Driver Implementations (Architecture Level)\n\n**Location:** `/workspace/arch/arm/src/stm32h7/`\n\nThe following STM32H7 drivers are available at the architecture level:\n\n| Driver | File | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| **ADC** | `stm32_adc.c` | Analog-to-Digital Converter |\n| **GPIO** | `stm32_gpio.c` | General Purpose I/O |\n| **PWM** | `stm32_pwm.c` | Pulse Width Modulation |\n| **Quadrature Encoder** | `stm32_qencoder.c` | Quadrature Encoder Interface |\n| **USB Device** | `stm32_otgdev.c` | USB OTG Device |\n| **USB Host** | `stm32_otghost.c` | USB OTG Host |\n| **I2C** | `stm32_i2c.c` | I2C Interface |\n| **SPI** | `stm32_spi.c` | SPI Interface |\n| **UART/Serial** | `stm32_serial.c` | USART/UART Serial |\n| **CAN/FDCAN** | `stm32_fdcan_sock.c` | CAN Bus (Socket CAN) |\n| **Ethernet** | `stm32_ethernet.c` | Ethernet MAC |\n| **SDMMC** | `stm32_sdmmc.c` | SD/MMC Card Interface |\n| **RTC** | `stm32_rtc.c` | Real-Time Clock |\n| **Timers** | `stm32_tim.c` | General Purpose Timers |\n| **QSPI** | `stm32_qspi.c` | Quad SPI Flash |\n| **LTDC** | `stm32_ltdc.c` | LCD-TFT Display Controller |\n| **Dual Core** | `stm32_dualcore.c` | Dual-core communication |\n| **RPMsg/RPTun** | `stm32_rptun.c` | Remote Proc Messaging |\n\n---\n\n### 4. Board-Level Driver Examples (from Nucleo-H743ZI)\n\nThe Nucleo-H743ZI board has more complete driver implementations that can serve as templates:\n\n**Location:** `/workspace/boards/arm/stm32h7/nucleo-h743zi/src/`\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `stm32_adc.c` | ADC setup and registration |\n| `stm32_gpio.c` | GPIO subsystem initialization |\n| `stm32_pwm.c` | PWM device registration |\n| `stm32_usb.c` | USB host/device initialization |\n| `stm32_spi.c` | SPI bus initialization |\n| `stm32_buttons.c` | Button/switch input |\n| `stm32_mmcsd.c` | SD card support |\n\n**Quadrature Encoder Example:** `/workspace/boards/arm/stm32h7/nucleo-h743zi2/src/stm32_qencoder.c`\n\n---\n\n### 5. Kconfig Configuration Structure\n\n**Main Board Kconfig:** `/workspace/boards/Kconfig`\n\n- **Line 1709-1715:** Nucleo-H745ZI board definition\n- **Line 3821-3823:** Kconfig source inclusion\n\n**Board-Specific Kconfig:** `/workspace/boards/arm/stm32h7/nucleo-h745zi/Kconfig`\n\nContains SMPS/LDO power configuration options:\n- `NUCLEOH745ZI_SMPS` (default)\n- `NUCLEOH745ZI_LDO`\n- `NUCLEOH745ZI_SMPS_LDO` (not supported)\n- `NUCLEOH745ZI_BYPASS` (not supported)\n\n---\n\n### 6. Key Files and Their Purposes\n\n#### Nucleo-H745ZI Specific Files:\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `include/board.h` | Clock configuration, LED/BUTTON definitions, pin mappings |\n| `src/nucleo-h745zi.h` | Board-specific macros, GPIO definitions, feature flags |\n| `src/stm32_bringup.c` | Board initialization (procfs, RPMsg) |\n| `src/stm32_boot.c` | Early boot initialization |\n| `configs/nsh_cm7/defconfig` | Cortex-M7 build configuration |\n| `configs/nsh_cm4/defconfig` | Cortex-M4 build configuration |\n\n#### Architecture Driver Headers:\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `arch/arm/src/stm32h7/stm32_adc.h` | ADC driver API |\n| `arch/arm/src/stm32h7/stm32_gpio.h` | GPIO configuration API |\n| `arch/arm/src/stm32h7/stm32_pwm.h` | PWM driver API |\n| `arch/arm/src/stm32h7/stm32_qencoder.h` | Quadrature encoder API |\n| `arch/arm/src/stm32h7/stm32_otg.h` | USB OTG definitions |\n\n---\n\n### 7. Documentation\n\n**Nucleo-H745ZI Documentation:** `/workspace/Documentation/platforms/arm/stm32h7/boards/nucleo-h745zi/index.rst`\n\nKey documentation points:\n- Dual-core support with CMake multi-image builds\n- Serial console via USART3 (PD8/PD9) for Cortex-M7\n- RPMsg UART for M4 core access\n- JLink recommended for flashing (not OpenOCD)\n\n---\n\n### 8. What's Missing in Nucleo-H745ZI\n\nCompared to Nucleo-H743ZI, the Nucleo-H745ZI board support is **minimal** and lacks:\n\n- ❌ ADC driver implementation (`stm32_adc.c`)\n- ❌ GPIO subsystem implementation (`stm32_gpio.c`)\n- ❌ PWM driver implementation (`stm32_pwm.c`)\n- ❌ Quadrature encoder implementation (`stm32_qencoder.c`)\n- ❌ USB driver implementation (`stm32_usb.c`)\n- ❌ SPI driver implementation\n- ❌ Button driver implementation\n- ❌ SD/MMC support\n- ❌ Sensor drivers (LSM6DSL, LSM303AGR, etc.)\n\nThe architecture-level drivers exist, but the **board-specific initialization code** for these peripherals is not present in the Nucleo-H745ZI `src/` directory.\n\n---\n\n### 9. Build System\n\n**CMake:** Preferred build system\n- Main: `boards/arm/stm32h7/nucleo-h745zi/CMakeLists.txt`\n- Source: `boards/arm/stm32h7/nucleo-h745zi/src/CMakeLists.txt`\n\n**Make:** Also supported\n- `boards/arm/stm32h7/nucleo-h745zi/src/Makefile`\n\n**Build Commands (from documentation):**\n```bash\n# Cortex-M7\ncmake -B build_h7m7 -DBOARD_CONFIG=nucleo-h745zi:nsh_cm7_rptun -GNinja\ncmake --build build_h7m7\n\n# Cortex-M4\ncmake -B build_h7m4 -DBOARD_CONFIG=nucleo-h745zi:nsh_cm4_rptun -GNinja\ncmake --build build_h7m4\n```\n\n---\n\n### 10. Summary of Key Locations\n\n| Component | Path |\n|-----------|------|\n| **Nucleo-H745ZI Board** | `/workspace/boards/arm/stm32h7/nucleo-h745zi/` |\n| **STM32H7 Arch Drivers** | `/workspace/arch/arm/src/stm32h7/` |\n| **Nucleo-H743ZI Examples** | `/workspace/boards/arm/stm32h7/nucleo-h743zi/src/` |\n| **Board Kconfig** | `/workspace/boards/Kconfig` (lines 1709, 3821) |\n| **Documentation** | `/workspace/Documentation/platforms/arm/stm32h7/boards/nucleo-h745zi/` |\n\nThe Nucleo-H745ZI board support exists but is basic - it provides dual-core boot, LED support, and RPMsg communication. Additional peripheral drivers (ADC, GPIO, PWM, encoder, USB) would need to be added following the patterns from Nucleo-H743ZI.\n</task_result>",
